2.0.1:

-- New Features --

[New] Alert template partials (files/alert/): 8 customizable {{VAR}} templates
      (4 plain text + 4 HTML) replacing sourced-bash alert.bfd; email-safe HTML
      with inline CSS and table layout; self-contained entry/summary cards;
      conditional sections via pre-computed variables for zero-logic templates
[New] Alert engine library (alert_lib.sh): safe {{VAR}} template renderer via
      awk ENVIRON substitution (no shell sourcing), HTML entity escaping,
      credential-redacting log sanitizer, IP reputation link builder
      (AbuseIPDB, Shodan, VirusTotal, IPinfo, GreyNoise), ASCII pressure bar
      visualization, color helpers for ban severity and pressure level,
      Unicode country flag emoji from 2-letter codes
[New] Pressure-to-response scoring model: exponential-decay scoring replaces
      fixed count thresholds; events add weighted pressure per rule, pressure
      decays via configurable half-life, bans fire when accumulated pressure
      exceeds trip point; cross-service aggregate trip; all math in native awk
      floats; old TRIG/TRIG_WINDOW configs auto-migrate
[New] Country pressure multipliers: auto-enabled when pressure-country.conf has
      entries; IP-to-country lookup via ipcountry.dat binary search;
      pressure-country.conf maps country codes to multipliers
[New] Per-rule pressure configuration via pressure.conf: PRESSURE_WEIGHT,
      PRESSURE_TRIP, SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL with three-tier precedence
      (rule file > pressure.conf > conf.bfd)
[New] Watch mode (-w/--watch): continuous daemon with configurable interval;
      SIGHUP config reload; systemd unit and SysVinit init script; dead-PID
      lock recovery for cron fallback
[New] Scan mode (--scan): full-log processing for all rules or a specific rule;
      supports dry-run, --max-lines=N, --scan-timeout=N; SCAN_MAX_LINES and
      SCAN_TIMEOUT config variables with startup validation
[New] Events CLI (--events): active pressure dashboard showing all tracked IPs
      with pressure scores, event counts, services, and ban proximity;
      per-IP detail with per-service breakdown; CIDR subnet reports;
      --json/--csv structured output for all modes
[New] Structured output (--json/--csv) for ban list (-l), events dashboard
      (-e), and attack pool reports (-a) including per-service breakdowns
      and unified IP reports
[New] FIREWALL="auto" with 8 backends: APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
      iptables, route, custom; auto-detection in priority order; nftables
      sets, iptables chain, firewalld rich rules, route blackhole
[New] Full IPv6 support: dual-stack detection, banning, and local address
      exclusion; BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 for firewalls requiring
      separate commands
[New] Temporary bans with auto-expiry (BAN_TTL); recidivism escalation
      (BAN_ESCALATE_AFTER/BAN_ESCALATE_WINDOW); escalation modes
      (none/linear/double with configurable cap); retry with exponential
      backoff; old names (BAN_DURATION, BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW) accepted
[New] Distributed attack detection: SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from same subnet
      triggers subnet ban; configurable IPv4/IPv6 masks
[New] Batched email alerts: single email per recipient per check cycle with
      enriched content (ban type, duration, recidivism, log excerpts);
      per-rule routing and suppression via RULE_EMAIL/SKIP_ALERT; atomic
      state file appends via flock; port-specific blocking via $PORTS
[New] Declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST> patterns,
      dual IPv4/IPv6 boundary-aware regex, and IGNOREREGEX per-rule exclusion;
      all rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines
[New] 22 new service rules (42 total): apache-auth, nginx-http-auth,
      mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube,
      plesk, dropbear, http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql,
      openvpn, phpmyadmin, gitlab, grafana, proxmox, lighttpd, mongodb, xrdp
[New] In-process tlog wrapper replaces external subprocess calls in all rules;
      eliminates fork+exec pairs per detection cycle
[New] Systemd journal reader with transparent fallback (16 of 34 rules);
      LOG_SOURCE config (auto/file/journal); cursor-based journal tracking;
      23 service-to-journalctl filter mappings via dynamic registry
[New] tlog_lib.sh shared incremental log reader: atomic cursor writes, optional
      flock-based locking, cursor validation with auto-reset, stale cursor
      protection, configurable first-run behavior, multi-format compressed
      rotation support, copytruncate handling, and generic decompression
[New] elog_lib.sh structured logging library with severity levels, classic
      syslog-style and JSON output formats, configurable via LOG_FORMAT and
      LOG_LEVEL
[New] CLI expanded from 4 to 21 flags: -S/--status, -C/--config, -R/--rules,
      -T/--test, --test-pattern, -l/--list, -u/--unban, -b/--ban, -c/--check,
      -d/--dryrun, -w/--watch, -V/--verbose, -v/--version, -h/--help,
      --flush-temp, --flush-all, --json, --csv
[New] Health check (-c/--check): validates config, log paths, firewall
      binaries, rule status, state directories, tlog, and active bans
[New] Run mode detection: structured identification (watch/systemd, watch/init,
      watch/manual, timer/systemd, cron, unknown)
[New] Verbose mode (-V/--verbose): per-IP pressure score, trip threshold,
      effective weight, and country multiplier shown during detection cycles
[New] Short and full help output: common commands shown with no arguments,
      full help via -h with semantic section grouping and examples
[New] bfd.1 nroff man page: OPTIONS, CONFIGURATION, PRESSURE MODEL, FIREWALL,
      RULES, FILES, SIGNALS, EXIT CODES; scan mode, events, structured output,
      upgrade guide
[New] bfd.bash-completion: context-sensitive tab completion for all CLI flags,
      IPs, rule names, config variables, and file paths
[New] importconf rewritten: awk-based config merge preserving user values;
      TRIG to PRESSURE_TRIP migration; thresholds.conf to pressure.conf
      per-rule translation; pre-2.0.1 backward compat; temp file cleanup trap
[New] install.sh: custom paths via INSTALL_PATH/BIN_PATH env vars; man page,
      bash completion, and SysVinit init script installation; auto-enable
      watch mode on fresh install; upgrade notice for watch mode on v1.5
      upgrades
[New] uninstall.sh: root check; service stop ordering; man page, completion,
      init script, backup directory, and custom log path cleanup
[New] Security functions: safe_source() validates ownership and permissions
      before sourcing; safe template expansion without eval; strict IP and
      email validation; rule name sanitization
[New] Per-cycle caching: ignore file merge for fast per-IP lookup; country
      lookup cache; pre-computed IP occurrence counts; timestamp formatting
      helpers replacing 30 inline date fallback patterns
[New] systemd units: bfd.service, bfd.timer, bfd-watch.service with
      SyslogIdentifier
[New] RPM packaging: FHS-compliant layout (/usr/sbin, /usr/lib/bfd, /etc/bfd,
      /usr/share/bfd, /var/lib/bfd); symlink farm at /usr/local/bfd for
      backward compat; sed transforms at build time; config(noreplace) for
      user-editable config; SysVinit service handling in scriptlets; single
      spec covers el7/el8/el9/el10
[New] DEB packaging: FHS layout with dh_link-based symlink farm;
      debhelper-compat 13; conffile protection; SysVinit init script included;
      install.sh-to-package migration; single .deb covers Debian 12 and
      Ubuntu 18/20/22/24
[New] Package build infrastructure: source tarball via git archive; native
      rpm/deb targets; Docker build containers for el7, el9, and Debian 12;
      10-category verification test suite covering FHS paths, symlink farm,
      config transforms, permissions, rule files, systemd units, and execution
[New] GitHub Actions release workflow: builds RPM (el7/el8/el9/el10) and DEB
      packages in parallel on tag push; creates GitHub Release with assets;
      build jobs gated by tag-push guard to prevent wasted CI on dispatch
[New] GitHub Actions CI pipeline: 10-OS Docker matrix with Buildx caching,
      bash -n syntax checks, and shellcheck static analysis; DEB maintainer
      scripts and bash-completion included in lint targets
[New] BATS test suite: 1200 tests across 36 files; shared helpers; parallel
      runner; 10 Dockerfiles; RFC 5737 test IPs; dedicated pressure model,
      country multiplier, watch mode, and scan mode test suites

-- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] Security: alert eval echo injection replaced with safe template
      expansion; show_config() eval injection guarded by whitelist;
      BAN_COMMAND template extracted raw preventing premature expansion;
      custom backend PORTS validated
[Fix] Security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files; state file
      operations wrapped in flock; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] Security: reject group-writable files in addition to world-writable
      in file safety checks; sanitize credential patterns in alert email
      log excerpts; validate IGNOREREGEX patterns before use
[Fix] Global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead holder
      immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] Watch mode: SIGTERM/SIGINT now properly exit the daemon; previous trap
      pattern let the while-true loop continue after cleanup
[Fix] Watch mode reload: unset config vars BEFORE re-sourcing to prevent
      stale values; clear pressure arrays; re-register journal filters on
      SIGHUP; re-derive log format variables; add fallback variable block
      for config-sourcing failures; pre-validate syntax and permissions
      before unsetting to prevent degraded daemon state
[Fix] Watch mode reload: config validation uses return instead of exit,
      preventing daemon crash on validation errors
[Fix] Upgrade path: importconf preserves pressure-country.conf, custom rule
      files, exclude.files, custom alert.bfd template, tlog cursor state
      files, and user-customized cron schedule on upgrade
[Fix] Upgrade path: health check validates UNBAN_COMMAND and UNBAN_COMMAND_V6
      binary existence
[Fix] install.sh: stop watch mode before upgrade to avoid restart delay;
      daemon-reload after sed; BINPATH parent dir creation; CWD portability;
      set sourced libraries to 640 permissions; chmod 750 on install directory;
      update-ipcountry.sh set executable and added to path replacement list
[Fix] nftables status: count actual set elements instead of reporting 1
      regardless of element count
[Fix] cron.daily: use dedicated lock file for flock to avoid write contention;
      check mkdir-based lock before rotating state files to prevent racing
      with running bfd process
[Fix] JSON escape: newline, tab, CR, backspace, and formfeed per RFC 8259;
      previously only backslash and double-quote were escaped
[Fix] Attack pool dedup: exact matching for rule names; previous substring
      match falsely deduped vsftpd/vsftpd2 and openvpn/openvpnas pairs
[Fix] Config validation: added OUTPUT_SYSLOG, EMAIL_ADDRESS, BFD_LOG_PATH,
      BAN_RETRY_COUNT, EMAIL_LOGLINES, LOG_FORMAT, LOG_LEVEL, and
      SCAN_TIMEOUT=0 validation; BAN_ESCALATION error mentions "exponential"
      as accepted deprecated alias
[Fix] show_config(): replace eval-based variable indirection with indirect
      expansion; BAN_COMMAND vars added to whitelist
[Fix] Rule variable leakage: IGNOREREGEX/PORTS/SKIP_ALERT/RULE_EMAIL now
      properly reset between rules via save/restore/clear helpers
[Fix] CLI exit codes: all dispatch branches validate args and propagate
      correctly; unknown flags exit non-zero
[Fix] Firewall backends: hardcoded paths replaced with command -v discovery;
      CIDR addresses pass through without extra suffix; guard against empty
      ip6tables binary with warning
[Fix] Symlink handling: stat -c calls add -L flag to dereference symlinks
      for package installs where files are symlinks to FHS locations
[Fix] Quiet mode (-q): remove stderr redirect so genuine errors reach cron's
      mail handler; stdout suppression sufficient for cron silence
[Fix] tlog: log rotation duplicate output; source safety validation; BASERUN
      install-time path replacement prevents cursor files in /tmp; unquote
      journal filter for multi-filter entries
[Fix] State files: restore 600 permissions after awk rewrite temp file;
      enforce 750 permissions on tmp/ and stats/ directories; log file
      creation uses chmod 640 to match logrotate directive
[Fix] Pressure alerts: format_alert_body read 11 fields from 12-field alert
      file corrupting email display; ATTACK_COUNT backward compat now uses
      pressure/1000 for sensible old-template display
[Fix] Display: status rounding normalized to match pressure computation;
      5 display functions used hardcoded trip default of 15 instead of 20
[Fix] Rule status: backward-compat variable mapping now called after sourcing
      rule files so old-style rules are counted correctly
[Fix] Ignore files: inline comments after IPs now handled correctly
[Fix] Subnet detection: defensive guard for masks below /8
[Fix] Pressure config: PRESSURE_WEIGHT and PRESSURE_TRIP values type-validated;
      non-numeric or zero values logged and skipped
[Fix] Rule fixes: postgresql impossible path test; vsftpd2 tag collision;
      modsec variable rename; missing SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd;
      ignore.hosts missing ::1 loopback
[Fix] IPv6: grep false-match replaced with exact matching
[Fix] Journal: filter key mismatch for rh_ipop3d; dispatch bypassed existing
      log files
[Fix] Tab completion: config_vars updated from old variable names to match
      current config whitelist
[Fix] Packaging: add tlog_lib.sh and elog_lib.sh to RPM spec and DEB
      manifests; add SysVinit service stop and deregister to all scriptlets
[Fix] Miscellaneous: POSIX == to = in test brackets; exit code quoting;
      attack pool regex to fixed-string grep; local address grep fix;
      WATCH_INTERVAL default syntax; sed -r to sed -E; UNBAN_COMMAND warning
      gated on FIREWALL="custom"; firewalld examples removed --permanent flag

-- Changes --

[Change] conf.bfd restructured into workflow-oriented sections (Pressure Model,
      Email Alerts, Banning, Custom Firewall Commands, Log Paths, Advanced);
      comments rewritten with worked examples; BAN_ESCALATION "exponential"
      renamed to "double" (old value still accepted); 4 internal-only
      variables moved to internals.conf; new variables documented as
      commented entries for discoverability
[Change] check() rewritten: pressure-based scoring replaces count-based
      thresholds; per-rule weight/trip/half-life; optional country multipliers;
      global cross-service pressure trip; per-run statistics;
      duplicate-ban prevention; per-cycle caching for country lookups and
      ignore lists; pre-computed IP occurrence counts
[Change] Rule variables renamed for clarity: REQ to PREREQ, LP to LOG_FILE,
      TLOG_TF to LOG_TAG, ARG_VAL to MATCHED_HOSTS; backward-compat shim
      for custom rules using old names
[Change] Rule validation rewritten to distinguish inactive rules from genuine
      misconfigurations; detection output now verbose-only with summary format
[Change] weights.country renamed to pressure-country.conf; PRESSURE_COUNTRY
      toggle removed in favor of auto-detection
[Change] Extract shared config_init() for startup and reload, eliminating
      duplicated config loading logic
[Change] Extract shared helpers: cleanup teardown, firewall retry with
      exponential backoff, file safety validation, pressure aggregation,
      events AWK processing
[Change] Structured output refactor: shared data helpers for ban list, attack
      pool, events, and IP search; each format (text/JSON/CSV) shares a
      single data source instead of reading state files multiple times
[Change] Logging: eout()/vout() rewritten as thin wrappers delegating to elog
      library; log calls assigned explicit severity levels; error and warning
      messages now write to stderr per UNIX convention
[Change] Email validation for addresses in config and per-rule RULE_EMAIL
[Change] importconf: defense-in-depth integer validation on legacy variable
      migrations and per-rule config values
[Change] tlog CLI rewritten with option parsing, subcommands, help system,
      path traversal rejection, and library security validation;
      backward-compatible positional interface preserved
[Change] tlog_lib.sh updated to canonical 2.0.2: rotation refactored with
      pipe fallback for disk-full; journal flock support; cursor validation
      hardening; CLI version cross-check
[Change] Shell modernization across all files: backticks to $(), $[expr] to
      $(( )), egrep to grep -E, for-cat to while-read, systematic variable
      quoting, hardcoded paths to command -v discovery
[Change] Remove dead deprecated functions and unused variables
[Change] sshd rule expanded from 3 to 8 patterns: keyboard-interactive, ident
      string, refused connect, max auth attempts, PAM failure
[Change] dovecot rule expanded from 2 to 5 patterns: Disconnected pop3/imap,
      submission-login auth failed; AUTH_LOG_PATH fallback for Debian/Ubuntu
[Change] proftpd rule expanded from 1 to 4 patterns: incorrect password,
      SECURITY VIOLATION, maximum login attempts
[Change] exim rules: expanded patterns, Debian support with exim4 binary and
      log path fallbacks
[Change] asterisk rules: SecurityEvent FailedACL pattern added; log path
      fallback for /var/log/asterisk/messages
[Change] postfix PORTS updated from 25,26 to 25,26,587,465 (submission/SMTPS)
[Change] sendmail rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: AUTH failure
[Change] http_401 and pam_generic rules: conservative defaults to prevent
      false positives
[Change] Attack pool (-a) extended with IP search report, per-service
      breakdown, ban status integration, and pressure column in top-25 reports
[Change] update-ipcountry.sh: download timeout, TLS fallback for legacy CA
      bundles, temp files in install path
[Change] install.sh: contextual progress output for every blocking stage;
      stage markers and summary block
[Change] UFW backend: comment marker on deny rules for identification;
      graceful fallback for older versions; status reports deny rule count
[Change] logrotate rewritten: copytruncate, weekly, compress, create 0640
[Change] cron.daily: flock-wrapped state rotation; copy-and-truncate preserves
      inodes; cursor files preserved; GPL header added
[Change] Default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] README wholesale rewrite: quick start, config reference, rule catalog,
      ban lifecycle, firewall backends, IPv6, CLI flags, scan mode, events
      dashboard, structured output, upgrade guide, troubleshooting
[Change] Version 1.6-1 to 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026
